# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for Qt's own synchronization, which TSan does
# not see because Qt is not instrumented (tests/README.md, Sanitizers; step 9
# of doc/nexttoonz_core_noqt.md, decision Q9-D). Only Qt's machinery goes
# here: a race in our code is fixed or recorded in
# doc/nexttoonz_known_issues.md, never suppressed.
#
#   TSAN_OPTIONS="suppressions=<this file> ..." <program>

# A queued signal's arguments: the emitting thread copies them
# (QMetaType::create) into the event it posts, the receiver's thread reads
# them when the event is delivered; QCoreApplication::postEvent and the event
# loop order the two, under a QMutex. Seen with TThread::Runnable's signals,
# emitted by the workers and delivered to the task's slots in the main
# thread.
race:QtMetaTypePrivate::QMetaTypeFunctionHelper
